      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "Your eyelids are pale inside.",
      "start_timestamp": "04:51",
      "end_timestamp": "04:53",
      "supports": [
        "physical_examination[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like anaemia of some kind, but I'd like to confirm. Let's get a full blood count, for pallor",
      "start_timestamp": "05:19",
      "end_timestamp": "05:32",
      "supports": [
        "procedures_and_investigations[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "I'll request a ferritin level, it'll help with possible iron deficiency.",
      "start_timestamp": "05:39",
      "end_timestamp": "05:44",
      "supports": [
        "procedures_and_investigations[1]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "EV_009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "speaker_role": "doctor",
      "transcript_text": "What I'm giving you is ferrous sulfate, 200 milligrams, once a day, for three months. That should help with possible iron deficiency. Iron can darken the stools and bother the stomach, so take it after food. Cut down on salt and fried food for now, it really does make a difference. A vitamin B12 level is something we might do if this doesn't improve next month.",
      "start_timestamp": "05:48",
      "end_timestamp": "06:15",
      "supports": [
        "clinical_assessment[0]",
        "procedures_and_investigations[2]"
      ]
    },
